#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221196 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221443 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "12ff3452-19b6-566a-8b39-ad880dee8858" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Effects of the Horizontal Scaling on Coefficients"}] :question/id #uuid "b8658f47-7f42-530a-a62e-1cc3144059aa" :question/math-academy-id "e-21835" :question/problem "Let $f(x)$ be the $2L$-periodic extension of a function $F(x)$ from $x\\in [-L,L)$ to $x \\in \\mathbb R.$ \nGiven that $L=2$ and $f(x) = \\cosh{(x+1)}$, find the $4$th cosine and the $4$th sine coefficients." :question/worked-solution "Recall that multiplying the argument of a function by $k \\neq 0$ represents the horizontal stretching of the corresponding graph by a factor of $\\dfrac{1}{k}.$\n\nNow, let $s=\\dfrac{\\pi}{L}x.$ Then, since $f(x)$ has a period of $2L,$ the function\n\n$$\ng(s) = f\\left(\\dfrac{L}{\\pi}s\\right)\n$$\n\nmust have a period of $2L \\cdot \\dfrac{\\pi}{L} = 2\\pi.$ \n\nThe Fourier series of $g(s)$ is\n\n$$\ng(s) \\sim \\dfrac{a_0}{2}+\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty}a_n\\cos(ns)+b_n\\sin(ns),\n$$\n\nwhere:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{0} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }g(s)\\,\\text{d}s \\\\ {a}_{n} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }g(s)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(ns)\\,\\text{d}s,\\,n\\ge 1 \\\\ {b}_{n} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }g(s)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(ns)\\,\\text{d}s,\\,n\\ge 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $s=\\dfrac{\\pi}{L}x$ and using the fact that $g(s) = f\\left(\\dfrac{L}{\\pi}s\\right),$ we get the Fourier series of $f(x){:}$\n\n$$\nf(x) \\sim \\dfrac{a_0}{2}+\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty}\na_n\\cos\\bigg(\\bbox[4pt, border: solid 1pt gainsboro]{\\dfrac{n\\pi}{L}x}\\bigg)+\nb_n\\sin\\bigg(\\bbox[4pt, border: solid 1pt gainsboro]{\\dfrac{n\\pi}{L}x}\\bigg)\n$$\n\nTherefore, $4$th cosine coefficient of $f(x)$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{4} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }g(s)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4s)\\,\\text{d}s \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(\\frac{L}{\\pi }s)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4s)\\,\\text{d}s \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-L}^{L}f(\\frac{L}{\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{L}x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{L}x)\\,\\text{d}(\\frac{\\pi }{L}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{L}{\\int }_{-L}^{L}f(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{4\\pi }{L}x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{L}{\\int }_{-L}^{L}f(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{4\\pi }{L}x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, $4$th sine coefficient of $f(x)$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{4} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }g(s)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4s)\\,\\text{d}s \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(\\frac{L}{\\pi }s)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4s)\\,\\text{d}s \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-L}^{L}f(\\frac{L}{\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{L}x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{L}x)\\,\\text{d}(\\frac{\\pi }{L}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{L}{\\int }_{-L}^{L}f(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{4\\pi }{L}x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{L}{\\int }_{-L}^{L}f(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{4\\pi }{L}x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $L=2$ and $f(x)=\\cosh(x+1),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{4} & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(x+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{4\\pi }{2}x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(x+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi x)\\,\\text{d}x, \\\\ {b}_{4} & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(x+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{4\\pi }{2}x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(x+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221197 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221444 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cb301102-1a82-5a81-bb11-b9fc56cd1dc7" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Constant Term For the Fourier Series"}] :question/id #uuid "ba1cc59e-66ed-58fc-a494-b949c7ed0a88" :question/math-academy-id "e-21836" :question/problem "$$\nf(x) \\sim \\dfrac{a_0}{2}+\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty}a_n\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{n\\pi}{2}x\\right)+b_n\\sin\\left(\\dfrac{n\\pi}{2}x\\right)\n$$\n\nLet $F(x)=3x^2-4x+1$ for $x\\in[-2,2).$ The Fourier series of the $4$-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is shown above. Find the exact value of $a_0.$" :question/worked-solution "For the Fourier series of a $2L$-periodic function, the constant term is given by\n\n$$\na_0=\\frac{1}{L}\\int_{-L}^{L} f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $L=2$ and $f(x)=3x^2-4x+1$ for $x \\in [-2,2).$ So, substituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{0} & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}(3{x}^{2}-4x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{[{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+x]}_{-2}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(({2}^{3}-2\\cdot {2}^{2}+2)-((-2)^{3}-2\\cdot (-2)^{2}+(-2))) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(2-(-18)) \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221198 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221445 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c3315887-ff5c-5fd7-93bd-a58800e378b8" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Coefficients For the Fourier Series"}] :question/id #uuid "823fc00b-48af-5e79-9dcc-5e519e81cd4f" :question/math-academy-id "e-21837" :question/problem "$$\nf(x) \\sim \\dfrac{a_0}{2}+\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty}a_n\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{n\\pi}{2}x\\right)+b_n\\sin\\left(\\dfrac{n\\pi}{2}x\\right)\n$$\n\nLet $F(x)=-5x+4$ for $x\\in[-2,2).$ The Fourier series of the $4$-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is shown above. Find the exact value of $a_3.$" :question/worked-solution "For the Fourier series of a $2L$-periodic function, the cosine coefficients are given by\n\n$$\na_n=\\frac{1}{L}\\int_{-L}^{L} f(x)\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{n\\pi}{L}x\\right)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $L=2$ and $f(x)=-5x+4$ for $x \\in [-2,2).$ So, substituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\na_3 = \\dfrac{1}{2}\\int_{-2}^{2} (-5x+4)\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{3\\pi}{2}x\\right)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe use the integration by parts: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=-5x+4\\, & ⇒\\,{u}^{′}=-5 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2}x)\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\frac{2}{3\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2}x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{3} & =\\frac{1}{2}(uv\\,{|}_{-2}^{2}-{\\int }_{-2}^{2}v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{2}{3\\pi }{[(-5x+4)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2}x)]}_{-2}^{2}-{\\int }_{-2}^{2}\\frac{2}{3\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2}x)\\cdot (-5)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{2}{3\\pi }[(-5(2)+4)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\pi )-(-5(-2)+4)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-3\\pi )]+\\frac{10}{3\\pi }{\\int }_{-2}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2}x)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{2}{3\\pi }\\cdot 0+\\frac{10}{3\\pi }\\cdot (-\\frac{2}{3\\pi }){[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2}x)]}_{-2}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(-\\frac{20}{9{\\pi }^{2}}[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-3\\pi )]) \\\\  & =-\\frac{10}{9{\\pi }^{2}}(-1-(-1)) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186222023 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221445 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c3315887-ff5c-5fd7-93bd-a58800e378b8" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Coefficients For the Fourier Series"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b9caddf0-8911-56aa-9169-d2dd07b18d7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{36}{5\\pi}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524678}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b9caddf0-8911-56aa-9169-d2dd07b18d7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{36}{5\\pi}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524678} :answer-field/id #uuid "3fefa1eb-6b94-56ab-91b1-2a7b190c1a7a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220816}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d8c14d18-5531-531f-b86c-3260af1f5733" :question/math-academy-id "q-340855" :question/problem "$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi }{3}x)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi }{3}x)\n$$\n\nLet $F(x)=6x+1$ for $x\\in [-3,3).$ The Fourier series of the $6$-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is shown above. Find the exact value of ${b}_{5}.$\n\n${b}_{5}=$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For the Fourier series of a $2L$-periodic function, the sine coefficients are given by\n\n$$\n{b}_{n}=\\frac{1}{L}{\\int }_{-L}^{L}f(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi }{L}x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $L=3$ and $f(x)=6x+1$ for $x\\in (-3,3).$ So, substituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n{b}_{5}=\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{-3}^{3}(6x+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{3}x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe use the integration by parts: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=6x+1\\, & ⇒\\,{u}^{′}=6 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{3}x)\\, & ⇒\\,v=-\\frac{3}{5\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{3}x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{5} & =\\frac{1}{3}(uv\\,{|}_{-3}^{3}-{\\int }_{-3}^{3}v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(-\\frac{3}{5\\pi }{[(6x+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{3}x)]}_{-3}^{3}+\\frac{18}{5\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{3}x)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5\\pi }(-{[(6x+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{3}x)]}_{-3}^{3}+6{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{3}x)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5\\pi }(-((6(3)+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5\\pi )-(6(-3)+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-5\\pi ))+\\frac{18}{5\\pi }{[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{3}x)]}_{-3}^{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5\\pi }(36+\\frac{18}{5\\pi }(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-5\\pi ))) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5\\pi }\\cdot 36 \\\\  & =\\frac{36}{5\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186550020 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221443 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "12ff3452-19b6-566a-8b39-ad880dee8858" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Effects of the Horizontal Scaling on Coefficients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23e03e47-e4e8-5fca-b00b-82be453f972c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549391} {:answer/id #uuid "86c4360f-61c6-544f-837f-69869e0595be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549567} {:answer/id #uuid "a678a72c-346e-543b-a426-99936f3a21b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549629} {:answer/id #uuid "cb286bc5-b920-5dea-9cb5-6caae099b3e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549694}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "23e03e47-e4e8-5fca-b00b-82be453f972c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549391} :answer-field/id #uuid "20357d5e-1bc8-5dd7-8db6-94cde34f7b98" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549816} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08c1423b-4b36-5a57-af95-274f05349530" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{n}{L\\pi }x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549326} {:answer/id #uuid "2cb1d5d8-50ce-55bc-914f-d72f4e722ac9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{nL}{\\pi }x" :db/id #edb/ref