i }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549516} {:answer/id #uuid "a8861f31-8fbf-503d-8ec9-a12bcfa47981" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{L}{\\int }_{-L}^{L}f(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{L}x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549634} {:answer/id #uuid "b7472e86-fb73-5765-9d14-67d33892a5fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{L}{\\int }_{-L}^{L}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549659}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "46db3448-44c8-5279-836f-d20ebb97a407" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{L}{\\int }_{-L}^{L}f(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{L}x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549462} :answer-field/id #uuid "d643ff56-169f-53e0-bd8e-d426b4ad8ecf" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549904}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "903d90ff-4e96-59f7-912a-24572f1e9b78" :question/math-academy-id "q-341780" :question/problem "Let $f(x)$ be the $2L$-periodic extension of a function $F(x)$ from $x\\in [-L,L)$ to $x\\in R.$\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\nThe Fourier series of $f$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({{field-1}})+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({{field-2}}).\n$$\n\nThe $7$th sine coefficient of the series is\n\n$$\n{b}_{7}={{field-3}}.\n$$\n\nGiven that $F(x)=x$ and $L=2\\pi ,$ the $7$th sine coefficient becomes\n\n$$\n{b}_{7}={{field-4}}\\,\\cdot \\,{{field-5}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that multiplying the argument of a function by $k\\ne 0$ represents the horizontal stretching of the corresponding graph by a factor of $\\frac{1}{k}.$\n\nNow, let $s=\\frac{\\pi }{L}x.$ Then, since $f(x)$ has a period of $2L,$ the function\n\n$$\ng(s)=f(\\frac{L}{\\pi }s)\n$$\n\nmust have a period of $2L\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{L}=2\\pi .$ \n\nThe Fourier series of $g(s)$ is\n\n$$\ng(s)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(ns)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(ns),\n$$\n\nwhere:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{0} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }g(s)\\,\\text{d}s \\\\ {a}_{n} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }g(s)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(ns)\\,\\text{d}s,\\,n\\ge 1 \\\\ {b}_{n} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }g(s)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(ns)\\,\\text{d}s,\\,n\\ge 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $s=\\frac{\\pi }{L}x$ and using the fact that $g(s)=f(\\frac{L}{\\pi }s),$ we get the Fourier series of $f(x):$\n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi }{L}x)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi }{L}x)\n$$\n\nTherefore, $7$th sine coefficient of $f(x)$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{7} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }g(s)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7s)\\,\\text{d}s \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(\\frac{L}{\\pi }s)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7s)\\,\\text{d}s \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-L}^{L}f(\\frac{L}{\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{L}x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{L}x)\\,\\text{d}(\\frac{\\pi }{L}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{L}{\\int }_{-L}^{L}f(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{L}x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{L}{\\int }_{-L}^{L}f(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{L}x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $L=2\\pi $ and $f(x)=x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{7} & =\\frac{1}{2\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{2\\pi }x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\pi }\\cdot {\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7}{2}x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317178 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221444 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cb301102-1a82-5a81-bb11-b9fc56cd1dc7" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Constant Term For the Fourier Series"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "264561c5-9799-51c9-a009-d1202a71c2b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315334}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "264561c5-9799-51c9-a009-d1202a71c2b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315334} :answer-field/id #uuid "79eafde2-60a3-502c-bcb3-a8d0d2d51c6e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316837}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e12f9894-53cb-5435-b393-ea7e08594626" :question/math-academy-id "q-341789" :question/problem "$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi x)\n$$\n\nLet $F(x)=6{x}^{2}+5x+1$ for $x\\in [-1,1).$ The Fourier series of the $2$-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is shown above. Find the exact value of ${a}_{0}.$\n\n${a}_{0}=$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For the Fourier series of a $2L$-periodic function, the constant term is given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{0}=\\frac{1}{L}{\\int }_{-L}^{L}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $L=1$ and $f(x)=6{x}^{2}+5x+1$ for $x\\in [-1,1).$ So, substituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{0} & =\\frac{1}{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}(6{x}^{2}+5x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[2{x}^{3}+\\frac{5}{2}{x}^{2}+x]}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =(2+\\frac{5}{2}+1)-((-2)+\\frac{5}{2}+(-1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{2}-(-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317180 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221444 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cb301102-1a82-5a81-bb11-b9fc56cd1dc7" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Constant Term For the Fourier Series"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "683d00f4-ccba-5afe-b662-8d0eabf9f77c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315704}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "683d00f4-ccba-5afe-b662-8d0eabf9f77c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315704} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a2d7910-bf07-556d-9ad6-5470d09fa25a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316720}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4ff4add4-78d2-5a7b-99c9-19043e538182" :question/math-academy-id "q-341791" :question/problem "$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi }{5}x)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi }{5}x)\n$$\n\nLet $F(x)=3{x}^{2}-4$ for $x\\in [-5,5).$ The Fourier series of the $10$-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is shown above. Find the exact value of ${a}_{0}.$\n\n${a}_{0}=$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For the Fourier series of a $2L$-periodic function, the constant term is given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{0}=\\frac{1}{L}{\\int }_{-L}^{L}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $L=5$ and $f(x)=3{x}^{2}-4$ for $x\\in [-5,5).$ So, substituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{0} & =\\frac{1}{5}{\\int }_{-5}^{5}(3{x}^{2}-4)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}{[{x}^{3}-4x]}_{-5}^{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(({5}^{3}-4\\cdot 5)-((-5)^{3}-4\\cdot (-5))) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(105-(-105)) \\\\  & =42.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186372794 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221444 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cb301102-1a82-5a81-bb11-b9fc56cd1dc7" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Constant Term For the Fourier Series"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8c493bcc-7040-54a8-b5d3-429d4cf6c165" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "58" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372796}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c493bcc-7040-54a8-b5d3-429d4cf6c165" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "58" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372796} :answer-field/id #uuid "66bca651-fc67-586c-a6ac-fc1254c6e1f1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372795}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e2e5c8de-82af-59f7-9831-0d0c36257889" :question/math-academy-id "q-341792" :question/problem "$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi }{6}x)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi }{6}x)\n$$\n\nLet $F(x)=2{x}^{2}+7x+5$ for $x\\in [-6,6).$ The Fourier series of the $12$-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is shown above. Find the exact value of ${a}_{0}.$\n\n${a}_{0}=$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For the Fourier series of a $2L$-periodic function, the constant term is given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{0}=\\frac{1}{L}{\\int }_{-L}^{L}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $L=6$ and $f(x)=2{x}^{2}+7x+5$ for $x\\in [-6,6).$ So, substituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{0} & =\\frac{1}{6}{\\int }_{-6}^{6}(2{x}^{2}+7x+5)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}{[\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3}+\\frac{7}{2}{x}^{2}+5x]}_{-6}^{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}((\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot {6}^{3}+\\frac{7}{2}\\cdot {6}^{2}+5\\cdot 6)-(\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot (-6)^{3}+\\frac{7}{2}\\cdot (-6)^{2}+5\\cdot (-6))) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}(300-(-48)) \\\\  & =58.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549993 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221444 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cb301102-1a82-5a81-bb11-b9fc56cd1dc7" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Constant Term For the Fourier Series"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f47cc34-1a40-54f8-8f21-1937b1207c8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549377}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1f47cc34-1a40-54f8-8f21-1937b1207c8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549377} :answer-field/id #uuid "b3e4d068-52a7-54b2-9f52-ab0c0b143b6e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549888}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bc08f5e3-6f0e-55df-87af-7552a06bb9df" :question/math-academy-id "q-341802" :question/problem "$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi }{2}x)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi }{2}x)\n$$\n\nLet $F(x)=-3x+3$ for $x\\in [-2,2).$ The Fourier series of the $4$-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is shown above. Find the exact value of ${a}_{0}.$\n\n${a}_{0}=$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For the Fourier series of a $2L$-periodic function, the constant term is given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{0}=\\frac{1}{L}{\\int }_{-L}^{L}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $L=2$ and $f(x)=-3x+3$ for $x\\in [-2,2).$ So, substituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{0} & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}(-3x+3)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{[-\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{2}+3x]}_{-2}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}((-\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot {2}^{2}+3\\cdot 2)-(-\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot (-2)^{2}+3\\cdot (-2))) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(0-(-12)) \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317182 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221444 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cb301102-1a82-5a81-bb11-b9fc56cd1dc7" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Constant Term For the Fourier Series"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1187d685-6f3a-5f79-ba01-9ff1d5115820" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315224}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1187d685-6f3a-5f79-ba01-9ff1d5115820" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315224} :answer-field/id #uuid "f4408d37-6153-5bfe-9cc4-a50aed7144fc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317124}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f681e236-f02a-536f-b3c2-833df650a871" :question/math-academy-id "q-341805" :question/problem "$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi }{8}x)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi }{8}x)\n$$\n\nLet $F(x)=-x+5$ for $x\\in [-8,8).$ The Fourier series of the $16$-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is shown above. Find the exact value of ${a}_{0}.$\n\n${a}_{0}=$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For the Fourier series of a $2L$-periodic function, the constant term is given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{0}=\\frac{1}{L}{\\int }_{-L}^{L}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $L=8$ and $f(x)=-x+5$ for $x\\in [-8,8).$ So, substituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{0} & =\\frac{1}{8}{\\int }_{-8}^{8}(-x+5)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}{[-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+5x]}_{-8}^{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}((-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {8}^{2}+5\\cdot 8)-(-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-8)^{2}+5\\cdot (-8))) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}(8-(-72)) \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549935 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221445 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c3315887-ff5c-5fd7-93bd-a58800e378b8" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Coefficients For the Fourier Series"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f308dd20-f66e-5ffb-861b-4ab8333e47b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{14}{3\\pi}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549769}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f308dd20-f66e-5ffb-861b-4ab8333e47b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{14}{3\\pi}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549769} :answer-field/id #uuid "50ebbed4-eb9c-5659-8b8c-f37f72666390" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549833}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "14280c74-af6e-5d18-9712-69501b60ddc5" :question/math-academy-id "q-341830" :question/problem "$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n}{2}x)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n}{2}x)\n$$\n\nThe Fourier series of the $4\\pi $-periodic extension $f(x)$ of the function \n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}5, & x\\in [0,2\\pi ) \\\\ -2, & x\\in [-2\\pi ,0)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis shown above. Find the exact value of ${b}_{3}.$\n\n${b}_{3}=$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For the Fourier series of a $2L$-periodic function, the sine coefficients are given by\n\n$$\n{b}_{n}=\\frac{1}{L}{\\int }_{-L}^{L}f(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi }{L}x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $L=2\\pi .$ Also, $f(x)=5$ for $x\\in [0,2\\pi )$ and $f(x)=-2$ for $x\\in [-2\\pi ,0).$ So, substituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{3} & =\\frac{1}{2\\pi }{\\int }_{-2\\pi }^{2\\pi }f(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3}{2}x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\pi }{\\int }_{-2\\pi }^{0}(-2)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3}{2}x)\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{1}{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3}{2}x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{2\\pi }\\cdot (-\\frac{2}{3}){[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3}{2}x)]}_{-2\\pi }^{0}+\\frac{5}{2\\pi }\\cdot (-\\frac{2}{3}){[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3}{2}x)]}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3\\pi }(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-3\\pi ))-\\frac{5}{3\\pi }(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3\\pi }(1-(-1))-\\frac{5}{3\\pi }((-1)-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3\\pi }+\\frac{10}{3\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{3\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549959 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221445 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c3315887-ff5c-5fd7-93bd-a58800e378b8" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Coefficients For the Fourier Series"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "824395f4-e1d3-5e0f-879c-0d03e310d7a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549559}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "824395f4-e1d3-5e0f-879c-0d03e310d7a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549559} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c30a88d-8e13-5d71-9185-007060f3d4e5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549846}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "46598e7e-81d3-578b-80cc-94d59f9707e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-341861" :question/problem "$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\n$$\n\nLet $F(x)=-4x$ for $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ).$ The Fourier series of the $2\\pi $-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is shown above. Find the exact value of ${b}_{2}.$\n\n${b}_{2}=$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For the Fourier series of a $2L$-periodic function, the sine coefficients are given by\n\n$$\n{b}_{n}=\\frac{1}{L}{\\int }_{-L}^{L}f(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi }{L}x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $L=\\pi $ and $f(x)=-4x$ for $x\\in (-\\pi ,\\pi ).$ So, substituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }(-4x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{\\pi }x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }(-4x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use the integration by parts: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=-4x\\, & ⇒\\,{u}^{′}=-4 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\, & ⇒\\,v=-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }(uv\\,{|}_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }-{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }(-\\frac{1}{2}{[(-4x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)]}_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }-{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }(-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x))(-4)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }(-\\frac{1}{2}((-4\\pi )\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi )-(4\\pi )\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-2\\pi ))-2{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }(-\\frac{1}{2}((-4\\pi )\\cdot 1-(4\\pi )\\cdot 1)-2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)]}_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }(4\\pi -(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-2\\pi ))) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\cdot (4\\pi -0) \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549978 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221445 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c3315887-ff5c-5fd7-93bd-a58800e378b8" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Coefficients For the Fourier Series"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88ed5bbc-d47f-5994-8b20-ac726fec6a85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549573}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "88ed5bbc-d47f-5994-8b20-ac726fec6a85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549573} :answer-field/id #uuid "a7ebfbb0-eafe-5de9-be9a-5eb3748e9483" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549880}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8c3f231c-8d0c-511e-b4f9-0d81c5e6659f" :question/math-academy-id "q-341863" :question/problem "$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi }{2}x)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi }{2}x)\n$$\n\nLet $F(x)=x+1$ for $x\\in [-2,2).$ The Fourier series of the $4$-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is shown above. Find the exact value of ${a}_{2}.$\n\n${a}_{2}=$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For the Fourier series of a $2L$-periodic function, the cosine coefficients are given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=\\frac{1}{L}{\\int }_{-L}^{L}f(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi }{L}x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $L=2$ and $f(x)=x+1$ for $x\\in [-2,2).$ So, substituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}(x+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{2}x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}(x+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use the integration by parts: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x+1\\, & ⇒\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}(uv\\,{|}_{-2}^{2}-{\\int }_{-2}^{2}v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{1}{\\pi }{[(x+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)]}_{-2}^{2}-{\\int }_{-2}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{1}{\\pi }[3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi )-(-1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-2\\pi )]-\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{\\pi }){[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)]}_{-2}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\cdot 0+\\frac{1}{{\\pi }^{2}}[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-2\\pi )]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{{\\pi }^{2}}(1-1) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186550007 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221445 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c3315887-ff5c-5fd7-93bd-a58800e378b8" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Coefficients For the Fourier Series"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "96e025f6-a797-5f53-bd93-ef33e6a27f03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549610}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "96e025f6-a797-5f53-bd93-ef33e6a27f03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549610} :answer-field/id #uuid "2afc926f-9cf1-5b4f-8748-f140b3012b4a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549821}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e5dc675f-f1b9-58e9-a567-64d8cd60aaaf" :question/math-academy-id "q-341873" :question/problem "$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi }{3}x)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi }{3}x)\n$$\n\nLet $F(x)=2x+7$ for $x\\in [-3,3).$ The Fourier series of the $6$-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is shown above. Find the exact value of ${a}_{1}.$\n\n${a}_{1}=$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For the Fourier series of a $2L$-periodic function, the cosine coefficients are given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=\\frac{1}{L}{\\int }_{-L}^{L}f(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi }{L}x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $L=3$ and $f(x)=2x+7$ for $x\\in [-3,3).$ So, substituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{-3}^{3}(2x+7)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe use the integration by parts: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=2x+7\\, & ⇒\\,{u}^{′}=2 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}x)\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\frac{3}{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{3}(uv\\,{|}_{-3}^{3}-{\\int }_{-3}^{3}v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(\\frac{3}{\\pi }{[(2x+7)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}x)]}_{-3}^{3}-{\\int }_{-3}^{3}\\frac{3}{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}x)\\cdot 2\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(\\frac{3}{\\pi }[13\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\pi )]-\\frac{6}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-3}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}x)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(\\frac{3}{\\pi }\\cdot 0-\\frac{6}{\\pi }\\cdot (-\\frac{3}{\\pi }){[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}x)]}_{-3}^{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(\\frac{18}{{\\pi }^{2}}[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\pi )]) \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{{\\pi }^{2}}(-1-(-1)) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
